  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adolescent Health Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  USAID&apos;s Adolescent Health Activity aims to accelerate reductions in adolescent marriage and childbearing in Bangladesh by addressing the root cultural and societal causes of these practices. The activity emphasizes supporting the transition of boys and girls (ages 10 to 14) into healthy adolescents and eventually adulthood by utilizing peer leaders and adolescent clubs to strengthen life skills, including financial literacy, building agency and negotiation skills, and preventing school drop out. Using FY 2024 funds, the activity will enable adolescents to exercise their right to delay marriage and early childbearing. The activity will engage community and social support systems, such as school and religious institutions, to delay marriage and early childbearing to facilitate healthy development of adolescents. The activity will work with relevant government ministries to strengthen essential services for adolescents and their families, including in the health sector, and institutionalize effective solutions. To create synergy and leverage opportunities, the activity will closely coordinate with the Strengthening Local Level Health Systems, Community Nutrition and Health, and the Mission&apos;s integrated youth activities.FY 2024 funding will contribute to Adaptation Indirect ($150k), Gender Equality ($1m), GBV ($500k),GBV-CEFM ($500k), GFS ($500k), Health Workforce ($300k), Cross-Cutting HSS ($1.25m),MHPSS ($100k), MSN ($500k), PGI-Indirect Digital ($200k),PGI-Indirect Health ($1m), PSE ($50k) and Youth and Emerging Leaders ($500k) issues. The activity will support the Joint Strategic Plan FY 2022-2026 (USAID and U.S. Department of State) Goal Three, with the U.S. government&apos;s Integrated Country Strategy Mission Objective of Improving inclusive and equitable health, education, and livelihood services, especially for women, youth, and marginalized groups.</narrative>
  </description>
